  "label": "User projected onto the scene of Rohingya refugee boys studying the Quran",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual scene of the boys studying, as the meme uses the image to evoke a specific emotional or ideological response. The user is implicitly invited to see the boys as representatives of a group (Muslim refugees) that is framed as incompatible with Western values, thus projecting the user's own biases or fears onto the scene. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the framing of the image and text creates an implicit projection where the user is positioned as a viewer who must confront or judge the scene, reinforcing the meme's harmful intent.",
